1
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:42,650
-Dad! Where are you going?
-Come.

2
00:00:44,227 --> 00:00:46,490
Don't you want to see
where your dad works?

3
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:49,570
Vittorio, what are you doing here?

4
00:00:49,730 --> 00:00:53,010
I brought my daughter
to see the courthouse.

5
00:00:53,170 --> 00:00:54,970
What a pretty girl!

6
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:59,490
In middle school
she got A-in Latin, A in Italian...

7
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:02,410
If she had a swank family
she'd have got all A .

8
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:05,250
This morning
I enrolled her in high school.

9
00:01:05,410 --> 00:01:07,690
-No less!
-Good morning.

10
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:10,090
-Good morning, Judge.
-Excellency, good morning.

11
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:13,338
-I'd like you to meet my daughter.
-This isn't the right time.

12
00:01:17,770 --> 00:01:20,610
That's Judge Iodice, he's a big wig.

13
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:23,210
He does
the most important trials in Naples.

14
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:24,770
He does them all.

15
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:27,450
This morning he was elsewhere.

16
00:01:27,610 --> 00:01:31,490
If you're a hammer, strike,
if you're an anvil, keep still.

17
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:34,050
We've to keep still, we're anvils.

18
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:46,650
Now pay attention,

19
00:01:46,810 --> 00:01:50,010
to go to school, you take the train
and get off at Montesacro.

20
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:55,050
From there you take the tram, the 21,
that takes you to Via dei Tribunali.

21
00:01:55,210 --> 00:01:57,410
Don't get it wrong, don't take the 12

22
00:01:57,570 --> 00:02:00,450
because that goes
to Piazza Nazionale, got that?

23
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:02,170
All right, Papa.

24
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:07,050
Alfonso!

25
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:10,250
-Good day.
-How are you?

26
00:02:10,410 --> 00:02:12,970
I took my daughter
to enroll at high school.

27
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:15,890
I'm showing her the route
from home to school.

28
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:17,610
-Pretty girl.
-Thank you.

29
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:20,890
-How are you?
-Everything's fine.

30
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:24,770
I'm going to the post office to pay
some bills for the counselor.

31
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:27,890
-What happened with him?
-That's another story...

32
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,250
Let’s just drop it.

33
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:34,090
-It ended up like I said?
-Like you said.

34
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:39,530
Lenù, where are you going?

35
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:58,850
What are you doing?

36
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:03,250
It's the sea.

37
00:03:03,410 --> 00:03:06,370
It was the first time I saw the sea.

38
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:09,650
I felt dazed by the light,

39
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:11,530
by the sound.

40
00:03:11,690 --> 00:03:15,890
It seemed that,
although the spectacle moved me,

41
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:18,210
many things, too many,

42
00:03:18,370 --> 00:03:22,210
were shedding around me,
unable to be grasped.

43
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:24,890
I thought about Lila,
about the two of us,

44
00:03:25,050 --> 00:03:28,930
about that day we went off
but then we came back.

45
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:32,450
At that moment
I thought about the two of us,

46
00:03:32,610 --> 00:03:36,970
about that day we went away together
and then we came back.

47
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:38,610
Do you remember?

48
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:45,050
And then my father there...
I'd never seen him like that.

49
00:03:45,210 --> 00:03:48,370
He says hello to everyone,
he always stops to talk.

50
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:52,530
I gotta tell Rino that we have to
accept the invitation to Gigliola's.

51
00:03:53,570 --> 00:03:57,690
I want to go, even if Rino
and my father can't come.

52
00:03:57,850 --> 00:04:01,050
-Weren't you listening to me?
-Of course, I was.

53
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:04,730
I wanna show you something.

54
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:11,650
Look, I got it from the library.

55
00:04:11,810 --> 00:04:13,410
HOW TO DANCE

56
00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:16,050
Come.

57
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:20,730
-What are you doing?
-Follow me.

58
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:40,490
Dip!

59
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:46,130
-I'll teach you.
-Do you know how to dance?

60
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:48,450
-He's really good.
-Come here.

61
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:52,610
Put your feet on top of mine.

62
00:04:53,730 --> 00:04:55,690
This is how I taught Lila.

63
00:04:56,690 --> 00:05:01,690
You got a lowcut dress

64
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:06,850
A hat with ribbons
and with roses...

65
00:05:08,490 --> 00:05:10,930
You don't know
how obsessed my sister is!

66
00:05:11,090 --> 00:05:14,810
If I show her a new step,
she practices it until she's got it.

67
00:05:14,970 --> 00:05:17,170
Just as well we don't have
a gramophone.

68
00:05:17,330 --> 00:05:19,810
Do you know what word gramophone is?

69
00:05:19,970 --> 00:05:21,530
No.

70
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:23,130
It's Greek.

71
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:27,930
Come here.

72
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:34,450
I loved you

73
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:39,250
You loved me...

74
00:05:44,290 --> 00:05:47,410
Later I'll write "gramophone"
for you with Greek letters.

75
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:51,770
She began studying Ancient Greek
even before I started high school.

76
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:54,690
She always did the things
I was supposed to do,

77
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:56,850
before me and better than me.

78
00:07:07,850 --> 00:07:09,170
Lovely ladies!

79
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:13,250
At the party Gigliola's mother
threw for her name day,

80
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:14,730
everyone was there.

81
00:07:14,890 --> 00:07:17,250
Giuseppina Peluso, Alfredo’s wife,

82
00:07:17,410 --> 00:07:19,530
with her children
Pasquale and Carmela

83
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:22,130
was under the same roof
as Maria Carracci,

84
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:23,690
Don Achilles’ widow,

85
00:07:23,850 --> 00:07:27,090
with her children Stefano,
Pinuccia and Alfonso.

86
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,730
For the first time,
the murderer’s children

87
00:07:29,890 --> 00:07:32,570
were in the same room
as the victim’s kids.

88
00:07:32,730 --> 00:07:34,650
Anything could have happened.

89
00:08:26,090 --> 00:08:27,810
So, what happens now?

90
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:53,330
Are you gonna dance?
Make me dance on my own?

91
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:56,570
Better that way.

92
00:08:56,730 --> 00:08:58,170
Go, Antonio!

93
00:09:59,810 --> 00:10:01,210
Rock'n'roll!

94
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:10,690
Why don't you go?

95
00:10:10,850 --> 00:10:12,970
I don't know how.

96
00:10:13,130 --> 00:10:15,210
But you practiced
rock'n'roll so much.

97
00:10:15,370 --> 00:10:18,170
I don't feel like it,
I want to stay here with you.

98
00:10:31,890 --> 00:10:35,570
-Why aren't you dancing?
-I can't do this one.

99
00:10:35,730 --> 00:10:37,730
Me neither, come on.

100
00:11:31,490 --> 00:11:33,210
Antonio, are you okay?

101
00:11:34,210 --> 00:11:35,770
Ada, come with me.

102
00:12:02,890 --> 00:12:04,570
You're good, Lila.

103
00:12:06,290 --> 00:12:07,850
Lila?

104
00:12:08,010 --> 00:12:09,810
Will you dance with me?

105
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:12,490
Carmela...

106
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:27,610
Michele, I don't want Pasquale here.

107
00:12:31,130 --> 00:12:33,050
Signora Spagnuolo.

108
00:13:23,450 --> 00:13:25,370
Pasquale, can I have a word?

109
00:13:50,090 --> 00:13:52,810
-Ada, we gotta go.
-What happened?

110
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:58,130
-Lenù, let's go.
-Let Lila finish and we'll go.

111
00:13:58,290 --> 00:14:01,650
No, we gotta go now. Rino's not here,
she's gotta come with us.

112
00:14:01,810 --> 00:14:03,450
Come on.

113
00:14:07,650 --> 00:14:09,210
Cocksucker!

114
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:36,050
Lila, we gotta go.

115
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:39,210
-All right, we'll go now.
-Wait, one more dance.

116
00:14:40,450 --> 00:14:42,810
-Let go of me!
-I'll take you home.

117
00:14:42,970 --> 00:14:45,050
-Let go of me.
-I told you to wait!

118
00:14:45,210 --> 00:14:46,730
Let go of me!

119
00:14:52,530 --> 00:14:54,530
-What's wrong?
-Let's go.

120
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:59,130
Do you believe this guy!

121
00:15:06,570 --> 00:15:08,330
-He touched me!
-Lila, we gotta go.

122
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:09,930
What an asshole!

123
00:15:10,090 --> 00:15:12,450
Just as well Rino wasn't there,
he'd be dead.

124
00:15:12,610 --> 00:15:14,250
You shouldn't have danced with him.

125
00:15:14,410 --> 00:15:17,010
Come on, let's join the others.

126
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:18,650
Come on, Lila.

127
00:15:28,650 --> 00:15:31,770
Sooner or later
they'll come down, sons of bitches!

128
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:35,050
They got money and tell the poor:

129
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:37,130
"Kick out the Pelusos!"

130
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:39,170
Pieces of shit!

131
00:15:39,330 --> 00:15:42,010
I left out of respect
for Signora Spagnuolo.

132
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:45,450
But now I'll wait for them,
I'm not afraid of their money.

133
00:15:45,610 --> 00:15:48,290
Everyone knows
where their money comes from!

134
00:15:48,450 --> 00:15:49,890
Lower your voice.

135
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:54,010
The Solara's bar is a hangout
for camorristiand loan sharks.

136
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:56,850
They ran a black market in there,

137
00:15:57,010 --> 00:15:59,650
they gathered votes
for the monarchists and fascists.

138
00:15:59,810 --> 00:16:02,850
-People don't forget.
-Pasquale, please.

139
00:16:03,010 --> 00:16:05,570
Carmela, I'm not afraid of anyone.

140
00:16:05,730 --> 00:16:09,890
Not even of Stefano Carracci,
who thinks he's God Almighty.

141
00:16:10,050 --> 00:16:14,450
The grocery store thrives with
the money of that rat Don Achille.

142
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,970
Cut it out.

143
00:16:16,130 --> 00:16:18,450
And Dad was right to kill him.

144
00:16:18,610 --> 00:16:20,690
Now I'll have to take care
of the Solaras.

145
00:16:20,850 --> 00:16:23,650
I swear to God, I'll wipe them off
the face of the earth!

146
00:16:25,050 --> 00:16:28,090
And you danced with that douchebag.

147
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:29,770
I didn't dance with anyone.

148
00:16:30,770 --> 00:16:32,850
I just danced,
what the fuck you want?

149
00:16:35,650 --> 00:16:38,090
I didn't dance with you either.

150
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:43,810
What the fuck
do you all want from me?

151
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:55,570
Pasquale's right, we can't always
keep our heads bowed.

152
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:59,810
We can't always stay under them.

153
00:16:59,970 --> 00:17:03,050
We gotta do something,
stand up to those assholes.

154
00:17:03,210 --> 00:17:05,050
You're scaring me.

155
00:17:05,210 --> 00:17:07,010
Let's all go home.

156
00:17:07,170 --> 00:17:10,650
Enzo, go if you want,
we're not budging.

157
00:17:42,170 --> 00:17:44,250
Okay, I get it.

158
00:17:45,410 --> 00:17:48,810
We're gonna deal with the Solaras
some other time.

159
00:17:48,970 --> 00:17:51,890
-Let's go home.
-Are you serious?

160
00:17:52,050 --> 00:17:54,770
Let's go home, Antonio.

161
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:57,570
But don't do that.

162
00:17:57,730 --> 00:17:59,330
Sorry, Pasquale.

163
00:18:01,090 --> 00:18:02,730
Never mind.

164
00:18:09,050 --> 00:18:12,810
People talk and don't know anything,
you know a lot of things.

165
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:16,770
-Don't make fun of me.
-I'm not making fun of you.

166
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:20,770
I mean it, you know lots of stuff.

167
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:22,450
Explain it to me.

168
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:26,610
What are monarchists? And fascists?

169
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:31,890
And what's the black market?

170
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:36,610
Certain people made money
from people's hunger during the war.

171
00:18:36,770 --> 00:18:41,010
They sold bread, pasta, coffee
at exorbitant prices.

172
00:18:41,170 --> 00:18:45,410
People were forced
to buy them to survive.

173
00:18:45,570 --> 00:18:49,410
Everything you see, the houses,
the cars, the buildings,

174
00:18:49,570 --> 00:18:54,010
they bought it all by fleecing
from someone else.

175
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:58,170
Do you understand?

176
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:01,410
Let's move away from here.

177
00:19:02,490 --> 00:19:04,810
Tell me, explain it to me.

178
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:09,410
It slowly became clear,
not only to me,

179
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:12,410
who had been watching her
since we were in first grade,

180
00:19:12,570 --> 00:19:16,050
but to everybody
that Lila had begun exuding a fluid

181
00:19:16,210 --> 00:19:19,570
that was not simply seductive,
but also dangerous.

182
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:27,450
When school started again,
on one hand, I suffered greatly,

183
00:19:27,610 --> 00:19:30,770
because I knew I wouldn't have
any more time for Lila.

184
00:19:30,930 --> 00:19:34,410
On the other, I was happy
to get away from her.

185
00:19:34,570 --> 00:19:38,530
It was a bloody war, lasted ten years,
with thousands of casualties.

186
00:19:38,690 --> 00:19:42,210
But we don't know
if this war really happened

187
00:19:42,370 --> 00:19:45,410
or if it's a war
that sums up all wars.

188
00:19:46,650 --> 00:19:48,490
Where was I?

189
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:53,050
Yes, when the Trojans decide
to leave Thrace.

190
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:56,570
Miss?

191
00:19:58,810 --> 00:20:01,890
The young lady in the fourth row,
I see you a little distracted.

192
00:20:03,250 --> 00:20:06,170
I still haven't learnt all your
names, there are so many of you.

193
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:08,330
What is your name?

194
00:20:08,490 --> 00:20:10,010
Elena Greco.

195
00:20:10,170 --> 00:20:12,610
Greco, why don't you continue?

196
00:20:12,770 --> 00:20:17,370
You tell me how the plot continues
when the Trojans leave Thrace.

197
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:22,690
The Trojans leave Thrace
and go to Delos,

198
00:20:22,850 --> 00:20:25,650
where they consult
the orocle of Apollo.

199
00:20:28,530 --> 00:20:29,850
Silence!

200
00:20:31,290 --> 00:20:33,130
It's pronounced "oracle".

201
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:38,890
In Delos that oracle
invites the Trojans

202
00:20:39,050 --> 00:20:41,050
to seek the ancient mother.

203
00:20:41,210 --> 00:20:43,850
So, the Trojans go to Crete.

204
00:20:44,010 --> 00:20:47,330
But Crete wasn't the land
the new city was to be build on,

205
00:20:47,490 --> 00:20:49,050
but Italy.

206
00:20:49,210 --> 00:20:52,490
In Italy too,
the Trojans encountered difficulties.

207
00:20:52,650 --> 00:20:56,690
This is the curse of the
Harpy Celaeno, from Book 3:

208
00:20:56,850 --> 00:20:59,890
"That you may reach Italy,

209
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:04,090
to Italy you shall go
and freely enter her harbors,

210
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:10,050
but you shall not gird with walls
your promised city,

211
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:15,130
until the wrong of violence
towards us sees you punished."

212
00:21:36,130 --> 00:21:37,450
Sarratore!

213
00:22:31,890 --> 00:22:33,210
Lenù.

214
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:37,930
Lenù, what happened?
Why are you going?

215
00:22:40,210 --> 00:22:42,370
Nothing, why?

216
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:44,850
You look awful... what happened?

217
00:22:46,010 --> 00:22:48,650
At school I said something dumb
about the Aeneid.

218
00:22:48,810 --> 00:22:50,610
Beautiful, the Aeneid!

219
00:22:51,610 --> 00:22:55,050
Wanna keep me company?
We'll eat a sandwich, I'm on my own.

220
00:22:55,210 --> 00:22:58,610
Papa and Rino went into town
to buy some stuff.

221
00:22:58,770 --> 00:23:00,290
Come in.

222
00:23:06,010 --> 00:23:08,010
Wanna go halves?

223
00:23:24,370 --> 00:23:27,770
-You know the Aeneid, too?
-Yes.

224
00:23:27,930 --> 00:23:31,290
The whole story of Dido,
who falls in love...

225
00:23:32,330 --> 00:23:35,050
who believes in love
even though she suffers.

226
00:23:35,210 --> 00:23:38,050
I think it means
that if there's no love

227
00:23:39,290 --> 00:23:42,770
not only does a person's life
have no worth,

228
00:23:42,930 --> 00:23:45,130
but nor does that of the whole city.

229
00:23:46,290 --> 00:23:49,450
At school we've only got
as far as Book 2.

230
00:23:49,610 --> 00:23:53,290
Aeneas abandons her,
as is always the case.

231
00:23:56,210 --> 00:23:59,410
-At school I saw Nino Sarratore.
-And you're telling me now?

232
00:24:00,810 --> 00:24:04,450
-He didn't even see me.
-But you gotta stop him.

233
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:07,450
And tell him about Melina,
how she is doing.

234
00:24:08,690 --> 00:24:10,970
So he'll tell his father.

235
00:24:13,330 --> 00:24:17,050
Is Marcello Solara interested in you?

236
00:24:17,210 --> 00:24:19,290
-Yes.
-And you?

237
00:24:22,130 --> 00:24:23,810
And Enzo?

238
00:24:23,970 --> 00:24:25,450
We're friends.

239
00:24:25,610 --> 00:24:27,770
And Stefano Carracci?

240
00:24:27,930 --> 00:24:31,090
-You think everyone is interested in me?
-Yes.

241
00:24:32,330 --> 00:24:35,050
Has Pasquale declared his feelings?

242
00:24:35,210 --> 00:24:38,690
-Are you nuts?
-You're always together.

243
00:24:38,850 --> 00:24:40,850
He walks you to the shop.

244
00:24:41,010 --> 00:24:44,690
He explains things
that happened in the past,

245
00:24:44,850 --> 00:24:48,210
he tells me what's behind
the wealth of certain people.

246
00:24:49,410 --> 00:24:51,810
The camorra, the black market.

247
00:24:53,050 --> 00:24:54,650
Loan sharking.

248
00:24:54,810 --> 00:24:59,050
We don't know anything,
we don't realize what's going on.

249
00:25:00,370 --> 00:25:04,810
Stefano's grocery store used to be
Pasquale's dad's carpentry shop.

250
00:25:05,850 --> 00:25:08,290
Don Achille made the money before.

251
00:25:08,450 --> 00:25:11,250
And the Solaras too, but how?

252
00:25:11,410 --> 00:25:13,410
No one could care less.

253
00:25:14,450 --> 00:25:18,090
And our families
spend in their stores.

254
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:19,770
That frightens me.

255
00:25:19,930 --> 00:25:23,570
No, we're afraid of things
we don't know.

256
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:26,810
The more we know,
the less we're afraid.

257
00:25:28,410 --> 00:25:29,730
Lila!

258
00:25:34,010 --> 00:25:36,010
Look who's here!

259
00:25:36,170 --> 00:25:39,810
Here's the little one.
See how she's grown?

260
00:25:39,970 --> 00:25:41,530
Lila was beautiful.

261
00:25:41,690 --> 00:25:45,410
Nino, if he saw her, would have
been entranced by her.

262
00:25:45,570 --> 00:25:48,490
I realized she was ahead of me
in everything,

263
00:25:48,650 --> 00:25:51,010
as if she were going
to some secret school.

264
00:25:51,170 --> 00:25:54,770
From that moment
I decided to buckle down and study,

265
00:25:54,930 --> 00:25:57,730
promising myself
I would never be less than her.

266
00:26:04,050 --> 00:26:05,370
Good morning.

267
00:26:08,090 --> 00:26:09,610
Be seated.

268
00:26:14,450 --> 00:26:17,970
Seeing as it's the last day
before the Christmas break,

269
00:26:20,170 --> 00:26:22,610
I have been clement.

270
00:26:23,730 --> 00:26:25,610
Do not fear.

271
00:26:34,970 --> 00:26:36,810
Greco, come here.

272
00:26:49,370 --> 00:26:51,410
Did you copy this translation?

273
00:26:51,570 --> 00:26:53,330
No.

274
00:26:53,490 --> 00:26:54,890
I swear.

275
00:26:55,050 --> 00:26:58,050
You know I can tell
if you really know things

276
00:26:58,210 --> 00:26:59,690
or if you've copied them?

277
00:27:01,090 --> 00:27:02,610
Yes.

278
00:27:02,770 --> 00:27:04,170
Anyway...

279
00:27:05,650 --> 00:27:07,410
A fine A.

280
00:27:09,170 --> 00:27:10,610
Thank you.

281
00:27:13,290 --> 00:27:14,690
Boselli.

282
00:27:17,410 --> 00:27:19,050
An utter shambles.

283
00:27:19,210 --> 00:27:20,530
Well done!

284
00:27:22,050 --> 00:27:23,570
Maiello.

285
00:27:28,690 --> 00:27:30,770
You too, have distinguished yourself.

286
00:27:51,170 --> 00:27:52,850
Elena!

287
00:27:54,730 --> 00:27:57,090
-Want to walk home together?
-Yes.

288
00:28:00,450 --> 00:28:02,970
Is it okay if we always
walk home together?

289
00:28:03,130 --> 00:28:06,090
I don't know, if you like, sure.

290
00:28:06,250 --> 00:28:07,890
Wait.

291
00:28:10,050 --> 00:28:12,090
Do you want to go steady with me?

292
00:28:19,970 --> 00:28:21,370
Did you understand?

293
00:28:22,930 --> 00:28:25,170
-Yes.
-And what's your answer?

294
00:28:31,610 --> 00:28:33,010
All right.

295
00:28:35,570 --> 00:28:36,890
Yes.

296
00:28:40,130 --> 00:28:44,610
I said yes to Gino only because
I wanted a boyfriend before Lila.

297
00:28:44,770 --> 00:28:46,370
I felt strong.

298
00:28:46,530 --> 00:28:50,330
I had gone beyond the neighborhood,
I was going to high school,

299
00:28:50,490 --> 00:28:53,690
I was with kids
who were studying Latin and Greek

300
00:28:53,850 --> 00:28:57,090
and not with bricklayers,
mechanics, fruit vendors

301
00:28:57,250 --> 00:28:59,370
and shoemakers, like her.

302
00:29:08,410 --> 00:29:10,970
Here I am!

303
00:29:11,130 --> 00:29:14,770
Rino, I'm going shopping
for the Christmas dinner.

304
00:29:14,930 --> 00:29:17,090
-I got a list this long.
-Me too.

305
00:29:17,250 --> 00:29:19,330
Lila, what about that thing?

306
00:29:22,570 --> 00:29:24,890
-You wanna see something?
-Yes.

307
00:29:27,850 --> 00:29:29,930
Keep it to yourself, though.

308
00:29:31,810 --> 00:29:34,690
Lila told me you're going out
with the pharmacist's son.

309
00:29:34,850 --> 00:29:36,210
It's not true.

310
00:29:36,370 --> 00:29:38,530
So, you like rich kids!

311
00:29:45,130 --> 00:29:47,050
Let her touch them.

312
00:29:50,890 --> 00:29:53,170
You know who can afford these shoes?

313
00:29:53,330 --> 00:29:56,330
Your sweetheart and your
father-in-law, the pharmacist.

314
00:29:59,210 --> 00:30:01,570
Bend them.

315
00:30:01,730 --> 00:30:04,770
-See how strong it is?
-It's true.

316
00:30:04,930 --> 00:30:07,730
-We need to make them stronger.
-Why?

317
00:30:10,930 --> 00:30:13,210
The seam is still too wide.

318
00:30:13,370 --> 00:30:15,890
And maybe they're too soft.

319
00:30:16,050 --> 00:30:18,970
How long would it take Dad
to see these mistakes?

320
00:30:23,090 --> 00:30:24,770
Why are you always giving me shit?

321
00:30:24,930 --> 00:30:27,330
Then let's try again with the water.

322
00:30:27,490 --> 00:30:30,370
No, Dad could come back any minute.

323
00:30:32,210 --> 00:30:34,650
You're scared to put it in water.

324
00:30:40,650 --> 00:30:42,570
You're very skilled, Rino.

325
00:30:43,730 --> 00:30:45,850
They turned out really well.

326
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:48,770
Tell that to that bitch
of a friend of yours.

327
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:51,250
See? She likes to fiddle around.

328
00:31:25,370 --> 00:31:26,690
Touch.

329
00:31:36,090 --> 00:31:38,530
-It's dry.
-It's wet.

330
00:31:38,690 --> 00:31:41,290
Only you feel the wet.

331
00:31:41,450 --> 00:31:43,010
Feel it.

332
00:31:53,810 --> 00:31:55,810
-It's a little bit wet.
-See?

333
00:31:55,970 --> 00:31:58,650
It was only in the water
for a moment and it's already wet.

334
00:31:59,890 --> 00:32:01,530
It's no good.

335
00:32:02,810 --> 00:32:05,610
We have to sew it all
from scratch again.

336
00:32:05,770 --> 00:32:07,490
What do we care about a little damp?

337
00:32:07,650 --> 00:32:11,370
You're in a hurry
and hurry's not good.

338
00:32:11,530 --> 00:32:14,490
-You wanna teach me how to live?
-That shoe is wet.

339
00:32:16,690 --> 00:32:19,170
Why do I have such
a stubborn bitch for a sister?

340
00:32:19,330 --> 00:32:20,650
Drop it, Rino.

341
00:32:20,810 --> 00:32:24,730
One day you say I'm doing it right,
the next that I have to start over.

342
00:32:24,890 --> 00:32:28,210
-It's just a pair of shoes.
-Be quiet, Lenù!

343
00:32:28,370 --> 00:32:29,770
Now you listen to me:

344
00:32:29,930 --> 00:32:33,730
I don't want to spend
my life being a servant!

345
00:32:33,890 --> 00:32:35,530
Let's get out of here, he's crazy.

346
00:32:35,690 --> 00:32:37,010
You hear me?

347
00:32:45,890 --> 00:32:48,650
He thinks he's close to being rich.

348
00:32:48,810 --> 00:32:53,210
He got it into his head to take out
a loan to buy fireworks for New Year's.

349
00:32:53,370 --> 00:32:57,370
He thinks the neighborhood
will think we're getting richer.

350
00:32:57,530 --> 00:33:01,170
-To make the Solaras jealous.
-But where's he getting the money?

351
00:33:01,330 --> 00:33:04,450
The Solaras have been preparing
the fireworks for a month.

352
00:33:11,010 --> 00:33:13,170
Pizza with escarole, then?

353
00:33:13,330 --> 00:33:15,970
Then I'll take a jar of honey
for the struffoli.

354
00:33:16,130 --> 00:33:18,370
Honey... perfect.

355
00:33:19,490 --> 00:33:21,410
This is going to take all day.

356
00:33:23,570 --> 00:33:27,090
This pasta stays firm
when you cook it that's a treat.

357
00:33:27,250 --> 00:33:30,450
-Then?
-Give me a pack of sugar.

358
00:33:30,610 --> 00:33:32,610
Sugar, there you are.

359
00:33:32,770 --> 00:33:35,130
Look here, look at this!
Anything else?

360
00:33:36,170 --> 00:33:38,250
You look really good.

361
00:33:38,410 --> 00:33:40,650
-No.
-Yes.

362
00:33:40,810 --> 00:33:42,410
Even with pimples.

363
00:33:43,690 --> 00:33:47,610
Is it the satisfaction
you get from school? Is it love?

364
00:33:47,770 --> 00:33:49,610
It's not love.

365
00:33:49,770 --> 00:33:52,450
I don't even know
if I have feelings for Gino.

366
00:33:54,330 --> 00:33:57,650
And you? Don't you want a boyfriend?

367
00:33:57,810 --> 00:34:01,330
I only want to think
about the shoe project.

368
00:34:01,365 --> 00:34:04,410
Alfonso!
Get the girls' shopping list.

369
00:34:09,210 --> 00:34:11,010
Lenù. Hi, Lila.

370
00:34:11,170 --> 00:34:12,965
-You got a shopping list?
-Of course.

371
00:34:13,010 --> 00:34:14,690
Give it to me.

372
00:34:21,614 --> 00:34:24,010
Which prosciutto
did Signora Lisetta buy?

373
00:34:24,032 --> 00:34:26,090
The rustic one.

374
00:34:26,250 --> 00:34:27,610
All right.

375
00:34:27,770 --> 00:34:29,530
Will you do a quarter for me, too?

376
00:34:29,690 --> 00:34:32,530
We understand each other, then.
Pinuccia!

377
00:34:34,370 --> 00:34:37,250
-Good evening.
-How pretty you've become.

378
00:34:39,450 --> 00:34:42,810
-Just as well Alfonso was there.
-Or we'd still be there.

379
00:34:44,770 --> 00:34:46,090
Lenù.

380
00:34:50,290 --> 00:34:53,050
Do you want to celebrate
News Year's Eve at my place?

381
00:34:54,970 --> 00:34:58,290
-Alfonso really wants you to.
-We've already got plans.

382
00:34:59,410 --> 00:35:01,570
We're with her brother
and the family.

383
00:35:01,730 --> 00:35:05,770
Invite Rino and your parents,
it's a big house.

384
00:35:05,801 --> 00:35:07,738
For the fireworks
we'll go up to the terrace.

385
00:35:07,810 --> 00:35:11,610
You know the Pelusos
are coming with us, right?

386
00:35:19,610 --> 00:35:21,810
Let's start over.

387
00:35:22,890 --> 00:35:27,610
Everybody come to me,
we'll dance, we'll drink spumante.

388
00:35:27,770 --> 00:35:29,250
As they say...

389
00:35:30,610 --> 00:35:32,530
New year, new life.

390
00:35:36,890 --> 00:35:38,610
Let me know.

391
00:35:42,370 --> 00:35:43,690
Stefano!

392
00:35:46,650 --> 00:35:49,690
-And the fireworks?
-What do you mean?

393
00:35:49,850 --> 00:35:51,410
We'll bring ours, and you?

394
00:35:53,290 --> 00:35:56,570
-How many fireworks do you want?
-Lots.

395
00:35:56,730 --> 00:35:58,170
Then come to me,

396
00:35:58,330 --> 00:36:01,450
when dawn breaks
we'll still be letting them off.

397
00:36:06,370 --> 00:36:07,810
Have a nice evening.

398
00:36:15,410 --> 00:36:17,370
Why is he inviting everyone?

399
00:36:18,370 --> 00:36:21,410
For you. See how he stared at you?

400
00:36:21,570 --> 00:36:24,370
No, he's doing it for you,
he's in love.

401
00:36:24,530 --> 00:36:27,250
To get you into his house,
he's even inviting communists,

402
00:36:27,410 --> 00:36:29,530
even his father's murderers.

403
00:36:32,490 --> 00:36:34,090
I see.

404
00:36:36,370 --> 00:36:38,810
He wants to do something
to stand out.

405
00:36:38,970 --> 00:36:40,730
What's Stefano's message?

406
00:36:40,890 --> 00:36:45,090
"My father was what he was,
but I'm not like him,

407
00:36:45,250 --> 00:36:47,770
enough with all this
neighborhood scheming."

408
00:36:47,930 --> 00:36:49,450
Lila's right.

409
00:36:51,050 --> 00:36:53,610
It's not just an invitation
to let off fireworks.

410
00:36:53,770 --> 00:36:56,610
He's saying that our fathers
did bad things,

411
00:36:56,770 --> 00:37:01,090
but we, their children,
should be different.

412
00:37:01,250 --> 00:37:05,770
You read too many books,
you never let your brain rest.

413
00:37:05,930 --> 00:37:08,170
What do you mean by "different"?

414
00:37:08,330 --> 00:37:10,930
Better, the opposite of the Solaras,

415
00:37:11,090 --> 00:37:13,410
who are worse
than their father and grandfather.

416
00:37:13,570 --> 00:37:15,370
I don't know.

417
00:37:16,570 --> 00:37:19,730
I think these are things
that you think, not him.

418
00:37:19,890 --> 00:37:22,130
Guys, you still haven't realized

419
00:37:22,290 --> 00:37:24,770
that Stefano Carracci is a clown?

420
00:37:24,930 --> 00:37:28,890
He's only inviting us to show off
in front of the neighborhood.

421
00:37:29,050 --> 00:37:31,730
What am I supposed to do?

422
00:37:31,890 --> 00:37:36,530
Don Achille sucked my father's blood
a little at a time.

423
00:37:36,690 --> 00:37:39,730
Papa was a good man and you know it,

424
00:37:39,890 --> 00:37:42,010
the carpenter shop was his life.

425
00:37:42,170 --> 00:37:45,250
Don Achille took advantage,
what was Papa supposed to do?

426
00:37:47,690 --> 00:37:51,250
You should see Mama's face
when she comes back from the prison.

427
00:37:54,450 --> 00:37:56,970
You're right, Pasquale,

428
00:37:57,130 --> 00:38:00,210
but that's precisely the problem.

429
00:38:00,370 --> 00:38:02,890
Do we want to stay like this
or do we want to change?

430
00:38:04,290 --> 00:38:06,610
And if we want to change,

431
00:38:06,770 --> 00:38:10,290
should we be on Stefano's side,
who suggests we change,

432
00:38:10,450 --> 00:38:14,130
or on the Solaras', who are drowning
the neighborhood in poison?

433
00:38:14,290 --> 00:38:16,810
I don't want to be on anybody's side.

434
00:38:16,970 --> 00:38:19,370
I want to see the Solaras dead.

435
00:38:25,410 --> 00:38:27,130
But think about it.

436
00:38:29,090 --> 00:38:31,770
If we let off the neighborhood
fireworks together,

437
00:38:31,930 --> 00:38:35,090
I want to see if the Solaras
still act like clowns.

438
00:39:13,210 --> 00:39:15,490
Good evening, come in.

439
00:39:15,650 --> 00:39:17,050
Hi, Lenù.

440
00:39:18,410 --> 00:39:19,890
Lila, good evening.

441
00:39:20,050 --> 00:39:22,370
Good evening, madam, all good?

442
00:39:22,530 --> 00:39:25,290
Good evening, Don Fernando.
Happy New Year!

443
00:39:27,250 --> 00:39:28,850
Hi, Ada.

444
00:39:29,970 --> 00:39:32,650
Signora Peluso,
it's a pleasure to have you here.

445
00:39:35,850 --> 00:39:37,450
Good evening, Stefano.

446
00:39:37,610 --> 00:39:39,250
-Good evening.
-Don Vittorio...

447
00:39:45,890 --> 00:39:47,530
Rino, all good?

448
00:39:51,010 --> 00:39:52,330
Thank you.

449
00:39:52,490 --> 00:39:56,650
Pasquale, it's a pleasure to have you
here, thank you for coming.

450
00:39:59,610 --> 00:40:01,050
I'll be right there.

451
00:40:10,850 --> 00:40:12,570
-Try it.
-Don't you like it?

452
00:40:16,170 --> 00:40:17,930
They're delicious.

453
00:40:19,330 --> 00:40:21,370
Be honest.

454
00:40:32,330 --> 00:40:35,210
Everybody, I'd like to propose
a toast to the new year

455
00:40:35,370 --> 00:40:37,770
and I'm very happy
to have you all here.

456
00:40:37,930 --> 00:40:41,970
But first, if I may, I'd like to
raise a glass to Signora Peluso.

457
00:40:42,130 --> 00:40:44,650
-And her children.
-Thank you, son.

458
00:40:45,770 --> 00:40:48,810
Carmela.
Pasquale.

459
00:40:48,970 --> 00:40:51,570
Thank you for coming.

460
00:40:51,730 --> 00:40:55,650
This year wonderful things
will happen to all of us,

461
00:40:55,810 --> 00:40:58,130
from the babies to the grandparents.

462
00:40:58,290 --> 00:41:00,570
Out with the old...

463
00:41:02,410 --> 00:41:04,810
for our own sake
and that of the neighborhood.

464
00:41:04,970 --> 00:41:06,290
Happy New Year!

465
00:41:06,450 --> 00:41:07,770
Cheers!

466
00:41:09,690 --> 00:41:11,210
Happy New Year.

467
00:41:16,810 --> 00:41:18,130
Thank you.

468
00:41:19,690 --> 00:41:22,250
-Stefano, what are we doing?
-Rino's right, it's ten minutes away.

469
00:41:22,410 --> 00:41:24,210
Let's go up!

470
00:41:24,370 --> 00:41:27,530
This is gonna be
a great year for everyone!

471
00:41:27,690 --> 00:41:29,370
We'll make the buildings
shake tonight!

472
00:41:29,530 --> 00:41:31,530
You'll make me shake like that.

473
00:41:31,690 --> 00:41:33,890
Or what kind of New Year's Eve is it?

474
00:41:38,850 --> 00:41:43,570
Three crates of rockets for us,
three of small rockets, pinwheels...

475
00:41:47,890 --> 00:41:50,810
Where are the kids? Here!

476
00:41:55,410 --> 00:41:57,730
-I'd like one of these.
-Here.

477
00:42:01,570 --> 00:42:03,530
Alfonso, you gonna help us, or not?

478
00:42:03,690 --> 00:42:06,290
You're just standing there
like a lug.

479
00:42:09,490 --> 00:42:10,810
Go and help Rino.

480
00:42:10,970 --> 00:42:12,290
Go, Alfonso.

481
00:42:13,450 --> 00:42:15,610
It's midnight!

482
00:42:15,770 --> 00:42:17,850
It's midnight!

483
00:42:18,010 --> 00:42:20,850
Ten, nine, eight,

484
00:42:21,010 --> 00:42:23,530
seven, six, five,

485
00:42:23,690 --> 00:42:26,250
four, three, two,

486
00:42:26,410 --> 00:42:27,850
one...

487
00:42:39,210 --> 00:42:40,530
Reload!

488
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:53,290
Mamma!

489
00:43:15,610 --> 00:43:19,090
The last night of the year
was like a night of battle,

490
00:43:19,250 --> 00:43:21,890
in the neighborhood
and all of Naples.

491
00:43:22,050 --> 00:43:25,610
The smoke from the gunpowder
made everything hazy.

492
00:43:26,730 --> 00:43:29,530
If there's a civil war, I thought,

493
00:43:29,690 --> 00:43:31,530
like the one between
Romulus and Remus,

494
00:43:31,690 --> 00:43:34,850
between Marius and Sulla,
between Caesar and Pompey,

495
00:43:35,010 --> 00:43:37,450
they would have
the same faces as these,

496
00:43:37,610 --> 00:43:40,810
the same expressions,
the same postures.

497
00:43:45,410 --> 00:43:47,330
Everyone in the neighborhood knew

498
00:43:47,490 --> 00:43:50,170
that what had happened until then
was very little.

499
00:43:50,330 --> 00:43:52,610
Facing us were the Solaras.

500
00:43:53,690 --> 00:43:56,610
Everyone said that
they'd have really let it rip

501
00:43:56,770 --> 00:43:59,650
only after all the beggars
had finished their little crackers

502
00:43:59,810 --> 00:44:01,810
and showers of silver and gold,

503
00:44:02,970 --> 00:44:07,530
only when the absolute masters
of the party were them.

504
00:44:26,930 --> 00:44:30,090
We'll burn you alive,
you and your kind!

505
00:44:31,450 --> 00:44:33,130
Sons of bitches!

506
00:44:42,690 --> 00:44:44,410
Let's fire it into his face.

507
00:44:46,930 --> 00:44:49,650
They're shooting at us!

508
00:44:49,810 --> 00:44:51,890
Guys, they're shooting at us!

509
00:44:54,450 --> 00:44:56,690
You've got nothing more to say?

510
00:44:56,850 --> 00:44:58,650
They did it on purpose.

511
00:45:04,210 --> 00:45:07,250
Slowly, slowly, don't be afraid.

512
00:45:09,090 --> 00:45:11,930
You come down too, come home.

513
00:45:17,770 --> 00:45:19,210
Don't stop.

514
00:45:30,610 --> 00:45:32,690
What's wrong, assholes?

515
00:45:32,850 --> 00:45:35,570
-They did it on purpose.
-Rino, calm down.

516
00:45:35,730 --> 00:45:38,410
Guys, we'll reload, don't worry.

517
00:45:44,450 --> 00:45:46,210
Pieces of shit!

518
00:45:49,090 --> 00:45:51,290
Pasquale, you're doing
three at a time.

519
00:45:52,330 --> 00:45:54,490
Here, put this in, too.

520
00:45:56,810 --> 00:45:58,930
Let's set them on fire!

521
00:45:59,090 --> 00:46:00,890
Rino, where are you going?

522
00:46:01,050 --> 00:46:02,930
Guys, reload them.

523
00:46:03,090 --> 00:46:04,530
There's plenty of them.

524
00:46:07,170 --> 00:46:09,530
Something was happening to her,

525
00:46:09,690 --> 00:46:13,370
what she later called
"dissolving boundaries".

526
00:46:16,050 --> 00:46:19,730
It was, she told me, as if
on a night of full moon over the sea

527
00:46:19,890 --> 00:46:23,410
an intense black stormy mass
advanced across the sky

528
00:46:23,570 --> 00:46:25,690
swallowing everything.

529
00:46:25,850 --> 00:46:27,730
Take these too, assholes!

530
00:46:29,610 --> 00:46:31,290
Do you see Rino?

531
00:46:32,610 --> 00:46:34,290
Look at him.

532
00:46:35,370 --> 00:46:38,450
Lila imagined, saw, felt,

533
00:46:38,610 --> 00:46:42,130
as if it were true,
her brother breaking up.

534
00:46:43,450 --> 00:46:46,250
In front of her very eyes,

535
00:46:46,410 --> 00:46:49,250
Rino’s customary expression gave way,

536
00:46:49,410 --> 00:46:52,370
showing her
what he was truly made of.

537
00:46:53,650 --> 00:46:57,610
Every second of that night
of celebration horrified her.

538
00:46:58,930 --> 00:47:00,690
Pieces of shit!

539
00:47:01,970 --> 00:47:05,130
Worthless pieces of shit!

540
00:47:19,450 --> 00:47:23,330
We showed them who's in charge
in this shitty neighborhood!

541
00:47:23,490 --> 00:47:27,490
You'll all burn together!
You'll all die together!

542
00:47:27,650 --> 00:47:30,050
Assholes!
That's what you are!

543
00:47:30,210 --> 00:47:33,610
You're not worth nothin'!

544
00:47:33,770 --> 00:47:35,370
Pieces of shit!

545
00:47:35,530 --> 00:47:37,370
-Fire!
-Show us!

546
00:47:37,530 --> 00:47:42,330
You'll all burn together, assholes!

547
00:47:42,490 --> 00:47:43,890
Pieces of shit!

548
00:47:46,930 --> 00:47:48,370
Assholes!

549
00:47:51,690 --> 00:47:54,370
Shitholes, take this, too!

550
00:48:20,850 --> 00:48:22,410
Are they done?

551
00:48:23,410 --> 00:48:25,050
Wait, I'm gonna get them.

552
00:48:25,210 --> 00:48:28,050
-Yes!
-They've run out.

553
00:48:28,210 --> 00:48:31,667
We showed them who's in charge
in this shitty neighborhood!

554
00:48:32,810 --> 00:48:34,970
Another one!

555
00:48:35,130 --> 00:48:37,530
Lila, come on.

556
00:48:37,690 --> 00:48:40,250
-We gotta do downstairs!
-They're shooting guns!

557
00:48:43,130 --> 00:48:44,610
Don't be a fool!

558
00:48:44,770 --> 00:48:46,330
Pieces of shit!

559
00:48:47,490 --> 00:48:50,290
Assholes!


